# A filter must stay above a map that changes the row count, otherwise it filters different rows.

admin 'create table test::t21 { id: int4, a: int4 }'
---
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
> |   id    |  namespace  |  table  |  created  |
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
> |  16388  |    test     |   t21   |   true    |
> +---------+-------------+---------+-----------+
>

query 'CALL rql::explain("from test::t21 map {id, s: gen::series(1, 3)} filter {id == 1}")'
---
> +-------+---------+----------+-------------+--------------------------------------------------+
> |  idx  |  depth  |  parent  |    kind     |                      detail                      |
> +-------+---------+----------+-------------+--------------------------------------------------+
> |   0   |    0    |   none   |   Filter    |               (id == Constant(1))                |
> |   1   |    1    |    0     |     Map     |  id, gen::series(Constant(1), Constant(3)) as s  |
> |   2   |    2    |    1     |  TableScan  |                    test::t21                     |
> +-------+---------+----------+-------------+--------------------------------------------------+
>
